\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The FLAIR model-to-data loop. A Model Owner develops against MIMIC-CLIF and submits a frozen model, code, or container. The Benchmark Committee reviews the task or model for reproducibility, clinical face validity, and security. The FLAIR Portal registers the approved artifact and distributes byte-identical code to participating CLIF sites. Each Site Lead or Data Steward runs the artifact locally in CLIF-WorkBench against site CLIF tables. Patient-level cohorts, features, and predictions remain inside the institutional boundary. Only aggregate, cell-suppressed JSON report bundles return to FLAIR. The leaderboard emphasizes per-site variation, including forest-plot style displays, rather than only a pooled scalar. Source: authors.}}{12}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:workflow}{{1}{12}{The FLAIR model-to-data loop. A Model Owner develops against MIMIC-CLIF and submits a frozen model, code, or container. The Benchmark Committee reviews the task or model for reproducibility, clinical face validity, and security. The FLAIR Portal registers the approved artifact and distributes byte-identical code to participating CLIF sites. Each Site Lead or Data Steward runs the artifact locally in CLIF-WorkBench against site CLIF tables. Patient-level cohorts, features, and predictions remain inside the institutional boundary. Only aggregate, cell-suppressed JSON report bundles return to FLAIR. The leaderboard emphasizes per-site variation, including forest-plot style displays, rather than only a pooled scalar. Source: authors}{figure.1}{}}
